.TH AVR\-ORG\-EMAIL\-DOMAIN\-VERIFY 1 "" "avr 0.3.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-org-email-domain-verify \- Check a claimed domain's DNS TXT record (admin only).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr org email-domain verify
[OPTIONS] DOMAIN
.SH DESCRIPTION
Check a claimed domain's DNS TXT record (admin only).
.PP
Each invocation performs a fresh DNS lookup. If DNS has not propagated, wait and run the command again.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr org email-domain verify example.com
    avr org email-domain verify corp.example.com --org acme
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    created_at, dns_record_name, dns_record_value, domain,
    organization_email_domain_id, verified, verified_at
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIDOMAIN\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-org-email-domain (1),
.BR avr-org-email-domain-claim (1),
.BR avr-org-email-domain-list (1),
.BR avr-org-email-domain-set (1)
